# Taskmark file conventions

When creating or editing Taskmark markdown:

- Accept legacy IDs like `T-297` and new IDs like `T-MM-a8f31c2d`.
- New IDs come from `scripts/allocate-id.py`; never use a shared counter.
- Static sizes only: XS=1, S=3, M=5, L=8, XL=13, XXL=21.
- There is no estimate or owner property. Actual is derived only from closed
  leaf Work log intervals; parent Actual sums descendant leaves.
- Create writes new item files only. Relationships come from `parent` and
  `epic`; never rewrite parent child lists or rollups.
- Execution writes only successfully executed leaf files, moves them directly
  from backlog to done, and never commits or pushes.
- Shelving writes only eligible task/bug leaves as `status: shelved`, preserves
  acceptance criteria and `cancelled: false`, never edits parent markdown, and
  never commits or pushes.
- Every product-work session appends Prompt & feedback on a matching leaf
  (open, or done if the work still belongs there). Create a new leaf only
  when nothing fits. Never log on epic or story parents.
- Parent rollups, logs, status, people, and dates are read-time derived.
- Never generate `INDEX.md`, `SIZING.md`, `VELOCITY.md`, a board `README.md`,
  a README changelog, or Last synced metadata.
- Board `CHANGELOG.md` is written only by `/tkmd-changelog` and
  `/tkmd-version`. Those commands do not commit.
- Follow the `taskmark-conventions` skill.
